import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse('{"title":"Module environments are parameters, not construction state","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Module environments are parameters, not construction state","type":"adr","date":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z","status":"proposed","applies_to":"`host` (`handl-plugin-lib-handl`), `kernel` (`handl-platform` —"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"handl/project/adrs/0156-module-env-as-parameter.md","filePath":"vendored/handl/project/adrs/0156-module-env-as-parameter.md"}'),a={name:`handl/project/adrs/0156-module-env-as-parameter.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="adr-0156-module-environments-are-parameters-not-construction-state" tabindex="-1">ADR-0156: Module environments are parameters, not construction state <a class="header-anchor" href="#adr-0156-module-environments-are-parameters-not-construction-state" aria-label="Permalink to “ADR-0156: Module environments are parameters, not construction state”">​</a></h1><p>trait surfaces only if needed)</p><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to “Context”">​</a></h2><p>A <code>.hnl</code> module&#39;s dependency environment is baked in at construction: <code>HandlModule::with_dependency_arc</code> appends <code>Arc&lt;dyn Module&gt;</code> to a <code>dependencies</code> vec and rebuilds the runtime builder. Two consequences:</p><ol><li><strong>No multi-env.</strong> The same source cannot be instantiated under two different dep bindings without rebuilding the module from scratch — and every sharing layer above (<code>TableImportResolver.cache</code>, <code>KitResolver</code>, <code>module_ref</code>, <code>ModuleLoader.cache</code>) is a name-keyed singleton, so one name can only ever mean one env.</li><li><strong>The env is implicit.</strong> The dep set a module <em>expects</em> lives in call-site order of <code>with_dependency_arc</code> calls, not in declared data; dep-name discovery is text-scanning (<code>str_handl_import_specs</code>, <code>collect_direct_imports</code>, <code>host_import_bindings</code>).</li></ol><p>The arrow-calculus framing suggests the cleaner model: a file is <code>Env ~&gt; Exports</code> — the environment is an <em>input</em>, applied, not assembled. That is the ML-functor shape (<code>export</code> already rewrites to record construction; <code>with_dependency_arc</code> is already parameterization, just imperative).</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to “Decision”">​</a></h2><p><strong>Lift the environment into a first-class <code>ModuleEnv</code> value and add <code>HandlModule::instantiate(&amp;self, env: ModuleEnv) -&gt; HandlModule</code>.</strong></p><ul><li><code>ModuleEnv</code> owns <code>{ dependencies: Vec&amp;lt;Arc&amp;lt;dyn Module&gt;&gt;, global_lookup: Option&amp;lt;Arc&amp;lt;dyn ModuleLookup&gt;&gt;, import_resolver: Option&amp;lt;Arc&amp;lt;dyn ImportResolver&gt;&gt; }</code> — the tuple <code>build_runtime</code> already threads through.</li><li><code>instantiate</code> produces a sibling module sharing the prepared source, language, and eval engine, with a <strong>fresh <code>module_id</code></strong>. Per-thread caches (<code>RUNTIME_CACHE</code>, <code>MODULE_VALUE_CACHE</code>, <code>AST_CACHE</code>) key on <code>module_id</code>, so env isolation costs nothing.</li><li><code>with_dependency*</code> / <code>with_global_lookup</code> / <code>with_import_resolver</code> remain as ergonomic sugar over the same path.</li><li><code>mod.fn</code> keeps dispatching through <code>ModuleLookup</code> — dep <em>functions</em> are native <code>Module</code> impls and cannot be arrow values today, so the registry boundary stays. (Scope-bound arrow environments — <code>str</code> as a record of arrows in lexical scope — are a separate, engine-level decision.)</li></ul><p><strong>Env signatures come from data, not text scans</strong>: a module&#39;s declared deps resolve via <code>ModuleResolver</code> against names read from <code>pkg.hnl</code><code>deps</code> (the existing manifest) rather than <code>str_handl_import_specs</code>-style source scanning where the manifest is authoritative. Text-scan extraction remains for in-body <code>import</code>/<code>from</code> statements (grammar-level, unchanged) and as the bootstrap path.</p><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to “Consequences”">​</a></h2><ul><li>Multi-env instantiation becomes a one-liner: <code>instantiate(env_a)</code> / <code>instantiate(env_b)</code> — enabling stub/mock/A-B dep surfaces for the research eval lanes without parallel module hierarchies.</li><li>No engine, grammar, or <code>.hnl</code> source change; the public <code>HandlModule</code> API is additive.</li><li>Name-keyed singleton caches above (<code>stdlib</code> tables, <code>KitResolver</code>, <code>ModuleLoader.cache</code>) still give one env per name — env-keyed variants are follow-up work where needed, not forced here. <em>Landed 2026-10-22:</em> <code>ModuleEnv</code> identity (<code>env_id</code>/<code>fork</code>, host <code>9971ceec</code>) + additive env-keyed variants — <code>get_handl_module_with_env</code>/ <code>resolve_with_env</code> (kit-core <code>33b25b9</code>), <code>module_ref_with_env</code>/ <code>load_hnl_file_with_env</code> (stdlib, host <code>a9a5ac22</code>). <code>ModuleLoader</code> carries no <code>ModuleEnv</code> (deps are <code>.handl.toml</code> paths, cache holds evaluated binding records) — nothing to key.</li><li><code>loader_parity</code>, <code>named_import</code>, and the <code>handl-runtime</code> module e2e tests pin the existing single-env behavior; <code>instantiate</code> adds tests for the multi-env case.</li></ul>`,12)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};